                        ],
                        "form": "die Gernegroße"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e4137887-ff60-3c61-ad42-78a25f466917",
                        "entry_id": "c78d4bb7-4fca-3d97-a6ad-cdca75b5907e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Person, die viel angibt und prahlt; jemand, der mehr darstellen möchte, als er tut"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial",
                            "outdated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "05ff0d00-7324-4922-a29a-a1b8bedfc05c",
                                "sense_id": "e4137887-ff60-3c61-ad42-78a25f466917",
                                "text": "Es ist allgemein bekannt, dass Herr Schmidt auch Gernegroß genannt wird."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6703d4b-5725-4b03-8828-a3789e262353",
                                "sense_id": "e4137887-ff60-3c61-ad42-78a25f466917",
                                "text": "„Der Internationale Währungsfonds in Washington lässt sich von geltungssüchtigen Gernegroß-Gestalten wie Alexis Tsipras und seinen haltlosen Forderungen nicht beeindrucken.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9cb10387-1bb9-4379-89ed-d321ab4fcc75",
                                "sense_id": "e4137887-ff60-3c61-ad42-78a25f466917",
                                "text": "„Die NPD […] ist ein Winzling, ein Gernegroß. Sie ist isoliert und geächtet.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "467b292d-6fb6-46c4-a828-bca41271b549",
                                "sense_id": "e4137887-ff60-3c61-ad42-78a25f466917",
                                "text": "„Der sich als liberal begreifende Teil der Öffentlichkeit […] sieht fassungslos zu, wie sich der Gernegroß mit der komischen Frisur einfach greift, was er begehrt. Donald Trump: »You can just grab them«“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2298969c-b9c4-4458-8ead-a0abfb54ee29",
                                "sense_id": "e4137887-ff60-3c61-ad42-78a25f466917",
                                "text": "„Bedingt durch diese Angeberei, gepaart mit der Großmannssucht eines Gernegroß, kann dem Saarländer [Oskar Lafontaine] deshalb eine gewisse Ähnlichkeit mit dem französischen Staatspräsidenten Herrn Sarkozy attestiert werden.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bd7f1f5c-9cfa-4c7f-b8bc-7c877bd93254",
                        "source_entry_id": "c78d4bb7-4fca-3d97-a6ad-cdca75b5907e",
                        "source_sense_id": "e4137887-ff60-3c61-ad42-78a25f466917",
                        "target_lang_word": "wannabe",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "wannabe",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2cf9646a-7252-36ee-8c79-27b4d2bed7fb",
                                        "entry_id": "87ca364b-c4a5-3c44-b0e6-c498dde1de2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who wishes to be someone or do something, but lacks the qualifications or talent; an overeager amateur; an aspirant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "attributive",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "informal",
                                            "often"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9509e3f6-8886-4355-a3e2-333f2ff8bf02",
                                                "sense_id": "2cf9646a-7252-36ee-8c79-27b4d2bed7fb",
                                                "text": "Hollywood's restaurants are full of wannabe actors waiting to be discovered."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "975b562b-06ec-4a2a-a9d5-2288fca19ae3",
                                                "sense_id": "2cf9646a-7252-36ee-8c79-27b4d2bed7fb",
                                                "text": "Most of the people Hiro knows are will-bes or wannabes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d33615fa-a81d-456f-ada3-7ea2391b1c58",
                                                "sense_id": "2cf9646a-7252-36ee-8c79-27b4d2bed7fb",
                                                "text": "Who the hell is that woman messing in my files? GET HER OUT OF HERE! I won't have my system messed up by some wannabe \"expert\" who'll be gone next week! Damn strangers who think they know it all but don't care about what we're really trying to achieve here."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06a0502e-7cff-4895-af64-4339c18fa589",
                                                "sense_id": "2cf9646a-7252-36ee-8c79-27b4d2bed7fb",
                                                "text": "He had the reputation of a wannabe hardman, riding his cousin's coattails."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "df5f0b6b-f6a6-3ae2-b7db-c1b0fc61a7dd",
                                        "entry_id": "87ca364b-c4a5-3c44-b0e6-c498dde1de2b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who wishes to be part of, or to assimilate to, a majority group of which they are not a member."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3913db5f-c404-47ae-bdc5-aa15101ecb33",
                                                "sense_id": "df5f0b6b-f6a6-3ae2-b7db-c1b0fc61a7dd",
                                                "text": "Bigger, mongrelly and black, he was clearly a Doberman wannabe."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "95092f48-4bd5-4b62-b7d0-615b2bdadeb1",
                        "source_entry_id": "c78d4bb7-4fca-3d97-a6ad-cdca75b5907e",
                        "source_sense_id": "e4137887-ff60-3c61-ad42-78a25f466917",
                        "target_lang_word": "braggart",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "braggart",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51a5f380-8ed2-363d-a1a6-c1b7b4e7f874",
                                        "entry_id": "d4263855-a5b4-3026-8f30-e680ffd76e90",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who constantly brags or boasts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45ee1c6c-31ca-432b-a027-b58643e30774",
                                                "sense_id": "51a5f380-8ed2-363d-a1a6-c1b7b4e7f874",
                                                "text": "O I could play the woman with mine eyes, / And Braggart with my tongue."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c28d36b-c048-4b66-bfc6-354dfea54a86",
                                                "sense_id": "51a5f380-8ed2-363d-a1a6-c1b7b4e7f874",
                                                "text": "Shallow water gives a great splash, and so a braggart has ever been contemptible in my eyes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0252817-6318-4df5-bf66-61e17cd51ecd",
                                                "sense_id": "51a5f380-8ed2-363d-a1a6-c1b7b4e7f874",
                                                "text": "A very good resolve to make and keep, if you would also keep any friends you make, is never to speak of anyone without, in imagination, having them overhear what you say. One often hears the exclamation “I would say it to her face!” At least be very sure that this is true, and not a braggart’s phrase and then—nine times out of ten think better of it and refrain."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "braggart",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "336ff6e6-9f5d-308e-9dcd-607807d12863",
                                        "entry_id": "861e2e01-a1f5-3da6-9ac2-773aa61cf329",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Characterized by boasting; boastful."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c1db0ef-a178-4608-a7ea-1eb19c556420",
                                                "sense_id": "336ff6e6-9f5d-308e-9dcd-607807d12863",
                                                "text": "O my fair Mistress, Truth! Shall I quit thee, / For huffing, braggart, puft Nobility?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebb6c33c-8136-4fda-81ff-ca2f33315b95",
                                                "sense_id": "336ff6e6-9f5d-308e-9dcd-607807d12863",
                                                "text": "Captain [Benjamin] Bonneville was delighted with the game look of these cavaliers of the mountains, welcomed them heartily to his camp, and ordered a free allowance of grog to regale them, which soon put them in the most braggart spirits."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22616bb0-e631-4830-8ad3-c9cdce94b965",
                                                "sense_id": "336ff6e6-9f5d-308e-9dcd-607807d12863",
                                                "text": "He took him on the long walks of which he was fond, and made him in some sort his humble confidant, talking to him of himself and his plans with large and braggart vagueness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d9d573c9-851c-4ebb-8020-36b8fc8d5631",
                        "source_entry_id": "c78d4bb7-4fca-3d97-a6ad-cdca75b5907e",
                        "source_sense_id": "e4137887-ff60-3c61-ad42-78a25f466917",
